dialogue trust_sage_5
title: The clean end
trigger: Trust sage level=5
once
speaker commander $commander
speaker hero $with

node open commander
  The Sage sits by the fire with the cord laid out straight along the ground, from the oldest knot to the free end, and is running a thumb along it, knot by knot.
  * You tied us in loose, the way you said. Still loose? -> tied_kept
    if: FlagSet sage:cord_tied
    do: AddTrust $with 5
  * The end's still clean. I told you it would stay that way. -> down_kept
    if: FlagSet sage:cord_down
    do: AddTrust $with 7
  * I told you to put that away. I was wrong. Show me. -> away_mended
    if: FlagSet sage:cord_away
    do: AddTrust $with 8
  * Counting again? -> counting
    do: AddTrust $with 3

node tied_kept hero
  Still loose. Every one of you. I check them every night, like a pulse. Sit down.
  -> count

node down_kept hero
  Still clean. I keep waiting to need it, and you keep not letting me. Sit down.
  -> count

node away_mended hero
  You were half wrong. It doesn't mend anyone. But you asked to see it, and that's the half that counts. Sit down.
  -> count

node counting hero
  Not counting. Finishing. Sit down.
  -> count

node count hero
  I counted them again tonight. The same number as under the spire. Not one new knot since I've been walking behind this wagon. On the road, that's the longest I've ever gone.
  -> wick

node wick commander
  The Sage's thumb stops on the first knot, the one worn smooth.
  * I promised we'd bring Wick down. That promise hasn't moved. -> promised_kept
    if: FlagSet sage:wick_promised
    do: AddTrust $with 9
    do: SetFlag sage:thread_carried
  * You told me it helped a little. Does it still? -> absolved_kept
    if: FlagSet sage:wick_absolved
    do: AddTrust $with 8
    do: SetFlag sage:thread_eased
  * I said Wick's choice was Wick's. I said it too easily. -> chose_mended
    if: FlagSet sage:wick_chose
    do: AddTrust $with 10
    do: SetFlag sage:thread_mended
  * Wick would know you never stopped counting. -> remembered
    do: AddTrust $with 6
    do: SetFlag sage:thread_remembered

node promised_kept hero
  I know it hasn't. I've watched you keep every other promise on this road. I stopped bracing for the morning you'd take it back.
  -> ask

node absolved_kept hero
  More than a little, now. I mended a child in the last town whose colour was going thin, the same as Wick's. Not all the way. But I stopped blaming my hands while I did it, and my hands were steadier.
  -> ask

node chose_mended hero
  Too easily. Maybe. But you said it straight, and I was angry, and then I kept thinking about it. Wick did choose. I can grieve a choice without having to have stopped it. That took me a long while.
  -> ask

node remembered hero
  Never stopped. No. That's what the knot's for. So Wick isn't one more name the stair swallowed without anyone noticing.
  -> ask

node ask hero
  So. The clean end. On the road, when a healer's cord is done, they tie one last knot and hang it on their own lantern. I don't know what the last knot should be. You're the one I'm walking behind, Commander. You pick.
  * Tie one for the first pilgrim who comes back down. It'll be us. -> first_down
    do: AddTrust $with 8
    do: SetFlag sage:end_first_down
  * Hang it on the wagon's lantern. This is your road now. -> wagon
    do: AddTrust $with 6
    do: SetFlag sage:end_wagon
  * Leave it undone. You've carried enough of the dead. -> undone
    do: AddTrust $with -2
    do: SetFlag sage:end_undone

node first_down hero
  The first one down. Nobody's ever tied that knot. I'll tie it now and leave it loose, and pull it tight the morning we walk off that stair.

node wagon hero
  The wagon's lantern. There's no road oil in it, and it's never once gone out. Wick would have laughed at that. Yes. Hold the light still, and I'll hang it.

node undone hero
  Undone. No. A cord with no end is just string. I'll leave it for now, since you asked. But I'll finish it someday, Commander, and the last knot will be yours whether you like it or not.
